{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     theme-toggle — the three-state control, for the sheet and any settings
     surface.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     SYSTEM IS A CHOICE, AND IT IS THE DEFAULT. A two-state toggle silently
     converts every visitor into someone with an explicit preference, and then
     their OS switching to dark at sunset does nothing for them. "Auto" is the
     option that keeps that working, so it is a real radio rather than an
     absence.

     Mono uppercase labels rather than glyphs: "auto" has no icon anyone reads
     correctly — every product draws it differently — and mono is this
     system's own material anyway.

     aria-checked is corrected by assets/js/nav.js from the stored choice on
     load. The sliding thumb is a pseudo-element positioned by :has() reading
     aria-checked, so there is no class and no JS for the animation.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<div class="ns-themetoggle" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{t "Colour theme"}}" data-ns-theme>
    <button type="button" class="ns-themetoggle__opt" role="radio" aria-checked="false"
            aria-label="{{t "Light"}}" data-ns-theme-value="light">{{t "Light"}}</button>
    <button type="button" class="ns-themetoggle__opt" role="radio" aria-checked="true"
            aria-label="{{t "Match the system setting"}}" data-ns-theme-value="system">{{t "Auto"}}</button>
    <button type="button" class="ns-themetoggle__opt" role="radio" aria-checked="false"
            aria-label="{{t "Dark"}}" data-ns-theme-value="dark">{{t "Dark"}}</button>
</div>
